# Enterprise

<Aside title="Placeholder">

This page is a stub. The enterprise distribution and its deployment guide are still being written.

</Aside>

The open-source server is built to be wrapped by a downstream distribution without forking core boot. An enterprise deployment uses the extension seams described in [Architecture](/self-hosting/architecture/#extension-seams) to add what a multi-tenant SaaS needs:

- A real policy engine and audit writer injected through `StateOverrides` before production validation runs, replacing the development stubs.
- Custom background workers registered with `spawn_worker` so they join the supervised drain.
- Additional protected routes mounted with `merge_http_protected`, behind the same edge and auth stack as core `/v1`.
- Full tenant separation across identity, registry, storage, policy, audit, observability, and evaluation.

The enterprise distribution, its licensing, and a deployment guide will land here.

## Related

- [Architecture](/self-hosting/architecture/#extension-seams): the seams an enterprise build extends.
- [SSO and OIDC](/self-hosting/sso-and-oidc/): federated identity, which enterprise deployments lean on heavily.
